    contraindications: ["Clarify GI obstruction, perforation, bleeding, pheochromocytoma, seizure disorder, Parkinson disease, history of tardive dyskinesia, or hypersensitivity."],
    interactions: ["Antipsychotics and other dopamine blockers raise EPS/NMS risk. CNS depressants increase sedation. Levodopa/dopamine agonist benefit can be reduced."],
    keyLabs: ["Renal function for dosing context; glucose trend in diabetic gastroparesis when relevant."],
    nclexTraps: ["Metoclopramide is not just an antiemetic; it moves the stomach. Do not use prokinetic logic when obstruction/perforation is possible."],
