    "**How to read the trend:** first-trimester gain is usually modest; most gain occurs in the second and third trimesters. A normal-BMI client often averages about 1 lb/week later in pregnancy, while overweight/obesity categories usually aim closer to about 0.5 lb/week, individualized by the OB plan.",
    "**Why it matters:** too little gain can point to hyperemesis, poor intake, food insecurity, eating disorder relapse, malabsorption, infection, substance use, or fetal-growth concern. Sudden rapid gain can be nutrition-related, but with edema, hypertension, headache, vision changes, RUQ pain, dyspnea, or proteinuria, think preeclampsia/fluid status.",
