      "**Nursing focus:** trend bilirubin/jaundice, INR/bleeding, creatinine/urine output, sodium, albumin, ascites, encephalopathy, variceal bleeding, infection/SBP, renal injury, medication hepatotoxicity, and transplant/hepatology instructions.",
      "**NCLEX trap:** MELD is not the same as Child-Pugh. MELD is lab-driven mortality/transplant-priority thinking; Child-Pugh also includes ascites and encephalopathy."
