      "**First nursing moves:** assess the client first: respiratory distress, SpO2, breath sounds, chest pain, tracheal deviation, subcutaneous emphysema, and whether the tube is still secure. Then check connections, dressing seal, tubing, and drainage system for loose or cracked areas per facility process.",
      "**Action direction:** keep the system below chest level, maintain the ordered setup, notify the provider for new/worsening air leak or patient deterioration, and prepare for imaging or system change if ordered.",
      "**NCLEX trap:** do not clamp routinely to 'fix bubbling.' Clamping can create tension physiology unless specifically ordered/protocol-directed for troubleshooting."
