      "**Meaning:** the pattern raises concern for cardiac tamponade, where pericardial pressure restricts ventricular filling and lowers cardiac output. The complete triad is often absent, so worsening shock, dyspnea, tachycardia, pulsus paradoxus, or electrical alternans still requires urgent evaluation."
